# Paths clang-format must never touch — see docs/BUILD_GUIDE.md Part 13.5.
#
# CI's format-check job runs `find firmware host \( -name "*.cpp" -o -name "*.h" \)` over a clean
# checkout, where none of these directories exist. Locally they do, and they hold third-party code
# (the STM32 Arduino core, STM32duino FreeRTOS, Adafruit and TinyGPSPlus) plus CMake's own probe
# files. Without this, running CI's command locally rewrites vendored sources inside the build tree.
#
# Patterns are globs relative to this file's directory, and `*` does NOT cross a `/` — so these
# need `**`. A pattern like `.pio/*` silently matches nothing below the first level.
**/.pio/**
**/build/**
**/build-*/**
